# Acceptance-smoke seal-test admission binding-name fix — apply ladder

The #180 seal's post-seal `loam amend apply --dry-run` HALTed with a false
MISSING_ADMISSION on the smoke component's OWN paths. Root cause: the smoke
seal-test named its admission tuple `_ALLOWED_PREFIXES`, but the loam-amend
seal-diff binding reader (`loam_amend.seal_diff.read_entries`, used by both
`loam amend apply` widening and `apply --dry-run` admission) matches a
top-level `allowed_prefixes` identifier — so the reader saw `BindingNotFound`,
admitted no component prefix, and flagged the component's own files. On a
SINGLE-component branch this never surfaced (the window was empty post-seal);
the #179/#180 interleaved multi-component branch put the component's own files
in-window and exposed it.

The fix renames the tuple to `allowed_prefixes` (same data, parseable name),
matching the workspace-bootstrap seal-test precedent. Root-cause fix — the
fence invariant test itself is unchanged in BEHAVIOUR (it still rejects any
non-admitted path); only the binding NAME changed so the harness reads it.

